    "presentation": {
      "chief_complaint": "Fever and fatigue",
      "hpi": "The patient is admitted with fever and fatigue, not with a finished explanation. Temperature is 38.40 C. Dental examination shows caries and periodontal disease. There is no prosthetic valve. Two blood-culture sets drawn before antibiotics grow Streptococcus oralis, reported susceptible to penicillin. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily is started after the cultures are drawn. Repeat cultures show no growth. Transesophageal echocardiography shows a mitral vegetation, mild regurgitation, no abscess, and preserved ventricular function. Cardiac surgery finds no current indication for an operation. Ceftriaxone 2 g intravenously once daily continues after discharge. Infectious diseases has not chosen the stop date and will do that at the visit. A four-week course is the usual native-valve range and is not yet the order. Hemoglobin fell from 13.6 to 11.9 g/dL without tachycardia or a transfusion. Aspirin and atorvastatin continue.",
      "review_of_systems": null,
      "presenting_symptoms": [
        "Fatigue",
        "Nausea"
      ],
      "symptom_duration": "one week",
      "symptom_course": "improving after treatment"
    },
